9 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $465K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $117K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Match Group, Inc. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $8.9B market cap on $3.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.76\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -10.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 11.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 52% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.25},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 29% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Communication Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Tinder's User Rebound Enough to Lift Match Group (NASDAQ:MTCH)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication/is-tinders-user-rebound-enough-to-lift-match-group-nasdaqmtch","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793874120.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.141,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Match Group (NASDAQ:MTCH) Turn Better Engagement Into Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication